  H^0(Z) = Z -[[2]]-> H^0(Z) = Z -[[1]]-> H^0(Z/2) = Z/2 -delta 0->
  H^1(Z) = 0 -0-> H^1(Z) = 0 -0-> H^1(Z/2) = Z/2 -delta [[1]]->
  H^2(Z) = Z/2 -0-> H^2(Z) = Z/2 -[[1]]-> H^2(Z/2) = Z/2 -delta 0->
  (maps in the groups' canonical generators; delta by the snake lemma: lift, apply d, divide by 2)
