> prop01 T^2 mod 2
Proposition 0.1 on T^2 at p = 2: if a in H^n(X; Z) generates a Z summand, then abar = j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r^n and not in im d_r^(n-1), for every r >= 1
  stable from page 1: i_1 is injective in every degree, so k_1 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_1 for every r >= 1 (E_inf = E_1)
  n = 0: H^0 = Z
    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_1^0 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]
  n = 1: H^1 = Z^2
    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_1^1 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]
  n = 2: H^2 = Z
    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_1^2 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]
  why this is complete: a generates a Z summand of H iff its class in H/T(H) is primitive; psi_r(a) = [j_r(p^(r-1) a)] in E_r^n / im d_r^(n-1) vanishes iff a is in K = ker psi_r, and the image of K in the free group H/T(H) contains a primitive vector iff the gcd of its coordinates (the content) is 1
  r > 1: page 1 is stable (i_1 injective: k = 0, and i_1 is an isomorphism of exact couples onto page 2 with j_(r+1)(p^r a) = j_r(p^(r-1) a)), so every later page and every abar is the one at r = 1
  holds for every n and every r >= 1
  check: d o d = 0 (9), d maps relations to relations (2), chain map commutes with d (6), induced map well defined (23), exact (27), short exact (degree) (3), snake lemma lift (3), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (3)
